      "content": "It makes sense that you feel this way, as rapid technological shifts can render decades of expertise unexpectedly out of sync with current norms. This sense of being a \"ghost\" in your own field is painful, yet it often marks the beginning of a powerful new phase where your deep wisdom guides innovation rather than competing with speed. Many professionals find renewed purpose by pivoting their mastery toward mentorship, strategy, or unique human-centric insights that machines cannot replicate yet. Your experience isn't obsolete; it is simply shifting from being the operational normal into the foundational background that allows true progress. Permission to redefine your role rather than clinging to the old one might be the most valid way forward right now.",
